# What `eas build` leaves out of the upload. EAS reads this file from the
# REPOSITORY ROOT only — a native/.easignore is never consulted — and when it
# exists it replaces every .gitignore in the tree. So the rules below are the
# .gitignore files' own, with one deliberate difference:
#
#   native/webroot/ is NOT ignored. It is the built web app — the checklist
#   itself — produced by `npm run build:native` at the repo root (in CI by
#   native-build.yml, which bakes the Dropbox key into it). It is gitignored as
#   build output; left out of the upload, the withWebroot config plugin fails
#   `expo prebuild` on the EAS worker, since it is what copies that tree into
#   the native projects.
#
# /native/ios/ and /native/android/ (expo prebuild output, regenerated on the
# worker) keep their leading slash, so the hand-written
# modules/widget-bridge/{ios,android} and widgets/android still go up.
#
# Keep this in step with the .gitignore files when they change. Check with
#   (cd native && npx eas-cli build:inspect -p ios -s archive -o <dir>)
# that the archive holds native/webroot/.

# .gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
.env
.env.local
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.coverage/
coverage/
docs/_build/
node_modules/
dist/
dev-dist/
.vite/
public/sw.js
public/workbox-*.js
.expo/
native/.expo/
native/android/
native/ios/
native/.metro-health-check*
.release-notes.md
native/store/copy.mts
native/store/store.config.json
native/store/screenshots/
native/fastlane/metadata/
tauri/target/
tauri/webroot/*
!tauri/webroot/.gitkeep
tauri/src-tauri/gen/

# native/.gitignore, re-anchored under native/ (rules the root file already
# applies repo-wide are not repeated).
/native/ios/
/native/android/
/native/targets/widget/Info.plist
